# Context

## Background
Implements the plan defined in docs/specs/human-and-agent-experience-plan.md
(commit 33d0ad8). One large commit because the CLI, daemon, dashboard, docs,
and skill bundle cross-reference each other; splitting would break
intermediate builds.

## Why This Way
- New packages (connection, protocol, reposnapshot, operations) keep the
  client and daemon on shared types instead of duplicated JSON shapes.
- Tailcat transport stays under experiments/ with its own go.mod until the
  plan's evaluation gate passes; it is not part of the main module build.

## Gotchas
- staticcheck in bin/tools was stale (built with go1.25 while go.mod
  requires go1.26.10). The Makefile only installs missing tools, so stale
  binaries must be deleted before make quality. This commit also fixes the
  19 findings the fresh staticcheck raised (dead ZFS helpers, unused
  wrappers, http status constants, tar.TypeRegA).
- Verified before commit: make quality green, go test ./... green.
